<!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-guide-intro","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section"} --><section class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-guide-intro"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-breadcrumb"} --><p class="fr-breadcrumb"><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/' ) ); ?>">Home</a> / Learn the Rosary</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":1} --><h1 class="wp-block-heading">How to pray the Rosary</h1><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-lead"} --><p class="fr-lead">A step-by-step guide, with room to begin.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The Rosary combines familiar prayers with reflection on the life of Jesus and Mary. A usual five-decade Rosary includes an opening set of prayers, five mysteries with ten Hail Marys each, and closing prayers.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:html --><nav class="fr-jump" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#steps">The steps</a><a href="#guided-prayer">Pray a decade</a><a href="#mysteries">The mysteries</a><a href="#questions">Your questions</a></nav><!-- /wp:html --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-guide-steps","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"steps"} --><section id="steps" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-guide-steps"><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-guide-aside","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-guide-aside"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">The steps, simply.</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>You don’t have to memorize everything first. Keep a guide nearby and pray at a pace that lets you reflect.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.familyrosary.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">Open the ministry’s printable guides</a></p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step-list","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step-list"><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} --><h3 class="wp-block-heading">Begin with the opening prayers</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Make the Sign of the Cross and pray the Apostles’ Creed. Pray one Our Father, three Hail Marys, then the Glory Be.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} --><h3 class="wp-block-heading">Name the first mystery</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Bring the mystery to mind and offer your intention. Pray an Our Father, ten Hail Marys and the Glory Be while reflecting. Many people add the Fatima Prayer.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} --><h3 class="wp-block-heading">Continue through five decades</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Repeat the pattern for each of the remaining four mysteries. Each decade is ten Hail Marys, with an Our Father before and a Glory Be after.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} --><h3 class="wp-block-heading">Close in prayer</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>After five decades, pray the Hail, Holy Queen and the concluding prayer, then make the Sign of the Cross. The linked complete guide includes the prayer texts.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-prayer-tool","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"guided-prayer"} --><section id="guided-prayer" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-prayer-tool"><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-prayer-settings","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-prayer-settings"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Pray one decade with us.</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Choose a mystery. Offer a quiet intention. Then move through the prayers at your own pace.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-small"} --><p class="fr-small">This guided decade is one part of the Rosary. Use the steps above for the complete five-decade prayer.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:html --><label class="fr-field" for="mystery-set">Mysteries<select id="mystery-set"><option value="joyful">Joyful</option><option value="sorrowful">Sorrowful</option><option value="glorious" selected>Glorious</option><option value="luminous">Luminous</option></select></label><label class="fr-field" for="mystery-number">Choose a decade<select id="mystery-number"><option value="0">1. The Resurrection</option><option value="1">2. The Ascension</option><option value="2">3. The Descent of the Holy Spirit</option><option value="3">4. The Assumption</option><option value="4">5. The Coronation of Mary</option></select></label><!-- /wp:html --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:html --><div class="fr-prayer-reader" data-prayer-reader>
<p class="fr-prayer-mystery" id="prayer-mystery">The Resurrection</p>
<p id="prayer-reference">Luke 24:1–12</p>
<div class="fr-prayer-progress" aria-label="Prayer progress"><span id="prayer-progress-text">Opening prayer · Our Father</span><progress id="prayer-progress" max="12" value="0">0 of 12 prayers completed</progress></div>
<h3 id="prayer-title" tabindex="-1">Our Father</h3>
<p class="fr-prayer-words" id="prayer-words">Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name; thy kingdom come; thy will be done on earth as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread; and forgive us our trespasses as we forgive those who trespass against us; and lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. Amen.</p>
<div class="fr-reader-controls"><button type="button" id="prayer-back" disabled>Previous</button><button type="button" class="fr-primary" id="prayer-next">Next prayer</button></div>
<button type="button" class="fr-reset" id="prayer-reset">Start this decade again</button><p id="prayer-status" class="fr-sr-only" role="status"></p>
<noscript><p>Enable JavaScript for the step-by-step controls, or use the complete printable guide linked above.</p></noscript>
</div><!-- /wp:html --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"mysteries"} --><section id="mysteries" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">The four sets of mysteries</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The days below follow a common weekly pattern. Sunday customs can vary with the liturgical season; you may choose another set.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:html --><div class="fr-mystery-list"><details><summary>Joyful mysteries <span>Monday and Saturday</span></summary><ol><li>The Annunciation</li><li>The Visitation</li><li>The Nativity</li><li>The Presentation</li><li>The Finding of Jesus in the Temple</li></ol></details><details><summary>Sorrowful mysteries <span>Tuesday and Friday</span></summary><ol><li>The Agony in the Garden</li><li>The Scourging at the Pillar</li><li>The Crowning with Thorns</li><li>The Carrying of the Cross</li><li>The Crucifixion</li></ol></details><details open><summary>Glorious mysteries <span>Wednesday and Sunday</span></summary><ol><li>The Resurrection</li><li>The Ascension</li><li>The Descent of the Holy Spirit</li><li>The Assumption</li><li>The Coronation of Mary</li></ol></details><details><summary>Luminous mysteries <span>Thursday</span></summary><ol><li>The Baptism of Jesus</li><li>The Wedding at Cana</li><li>The Proclamation of the Kingdom</li><li>The Transfiguration</li><li>The Institution of the Eucharist</li></ol></details></div><!-- /wp:html --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"questions"} --><section id="questions" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Questions you might be bringing</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:html --><div class="fr-questions"><details><summary>Do I have to know every prayer?</summary><p>No. Read the words from a guide as you go. You can learn the prayers through repetition.</p></details><details><summary>Can I begin with one decade?</summary><p>Yes. A decade gives you a manageable place to begin and learn the rhythm. It is part of the Rosary, not a replacement name for all five decades.</p></details><details><summary>What if my children can’t sit still?</summary><p>Give them a simple role, such as naming an intention or counting a decade. Try a short shared moment and build a routine that your family can grow into.</p></details><details><summary>Where can I find a guide in another language?</summary><p>The existing Family Rosary how-to page offers English, Spanish and Portuguese PDF guides. <a class="text-link" href="https://www.familyrosary.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">Open those guides</a></p></details></div><!-- /wp:html --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-source-note"} --><p class="fr-source-note">Sources for the order and mysteries: <a class="text-link" href="https://www.usccb.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">USCCB Rosary guide</a> and <a class="text-link" href="https://www.familyrosary.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">Family Rosary’s existing guide</a>. Proposed wording awaits ministry editorial review.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></section><!-- /wp:group -->
